    "text": "<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> average force is exerted by a light wave on a non-reflecting surface of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> area during <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>min</mi></math> of time span, the energy flux of light just before it falls on the surface is _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>(Round off to the Nearest Integer), (Assume complete absorption and normal&nbsp;incidence conditions are there)</p>"
